0..56 Comment "// Two nestings of one chain of paths are one composite."
57..59 Comment "//"
60..139 Comment "// A proof then writes `here` where it would cite an associator, and the theory"
140..167 Comment "// adjoins no cell for one."
168..170 Comment "//"
171..245 Comment "// A transport along a stuck composite moves its operand along each of the"
246..325 Comment "// composite\'s paths in turn, in evaluation and in the kernel. Every nesting of"
326..407 Comment "// a chain so reaches the left-nested `then` fold the unbiased composite carries."
408..410 Comment "//"
411..482 Comment "// - see: `compose-chain.gandr` — the unbiased composite and its fold"
483..536 Comment "// - see: `then.gandr` — the composite of two paths"
538..576 Comment "// The circle, its point and its loop."
